segment.source:
::...and faint. 

You open your eyes even though you are sure they had already-- 

No, you remember it now: You fainted. You remember... horror. Utter horror. But you must look again no matter what. As you lay those fearful eyes upon yourself again, the shock surges through you like the energy that woke you from your timeless slumber; the feeling shakes you not unlike a bowl of living jelly... from which you, in fact, might not be so different.::&lt;end&gt;

